# Integrations

The harness works standalone, but light up more when an issue tracker and git host are
wired. Every integration **degrades gracefully**: if the connection is missing, skills
keep working and only the status-sync side effects drop off.

## Issue tracker — {{ issue_tracker }}

{% if issue_tracker == "linear" -%}
Work is tracked in **Linear**. Conventions:

- Non-trivial work starts as a Linear issue.
- Branch: `<type>/{{ issue_prefix | lower }}-<n>-<slug>`.
- PR title ends with `({{ issue_prefix }}-N)`; PR body has a `Closes {{ issue_prefix }}-N` line.
- Plan/SDD skills pull the issue, execute, and move its status.

**Degradation:** without the Linear MCP connected, the skills skip status updates —
code, branch, and PR still happen; you move the issue by hand.
{%- elif issue_tracker == "github" -%}
Work is tracked in **GitHub Issues**. Conventions:

- Non-trivial work starts as an issue.
- Branch: `<type>/{{ issue_prefix | lower }}-<n>-<slug>`.
- PR title ends with `({{ issue_prefix }}-N)`; PR body has a `Closes #N` line so merge
  closes the issue.

**Degradation:** without API access, the skills skip issue reads/writes — the local
flow (branch → commit → PR) is unaffected.
{%- else -%}
No issue tracker is configured. The plan and SDD flows run **local-only**:
branch → commit → PR, with no external status sync. To add one later, set
`issue_tracker` and re-run `copier update`.
{%- endif %}

## Git host — {{ git_host }}

{% if git_host == "github" -%}
Pull requests target **GitHub**. CI runs via `.github/workflows/`.
{% if include_pr_review_ai -%}
The AI PR-review workflow (`pr-review.yml`) posts inline review comments on PRs against
the default branch — assistive, not a merge gate.
{% endif -%}
{%- elif git_host == "gitlab" -%}
Merge requests target **GitLab**. Port the workflow definitions in `.github/workflows/`
to `.gitlab-ci.yml` — the task seam (`{{ task_runner }}`) is unchanged, so only the CI
wrapper differs.
{%- else -%}
No git host is configured. Adapt the CI definitions under `.github/workflows/` to your
host; they only ever call task-runner recipes, so the port is mechanical.
{%- endif %}

## Agent surface

Adapters are generated for every supported tool regardless of `primary_agent`
({{ primary_agent }}):

| Tool | Entry point |
| --- | --- |
| Claude Code | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (imports `AGENTS.md`) + `.claude/skills/` |
| Codex / Cursor / Gemini / Aider / Zed | `AGENTS.md` (native) |
| GitHub Copilot | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` + `.github/instructions/` |

Keep `AGENTS.md` as the single source; regenerate adapters with
`{% if task_runner == 'just' %}just sync-adapters{% else %}node tools/sync-adapters.mjs{% endif %}`.
